[
    {
        "content": "<p>I just wrote a command and would like to know if people are interested in seeing this command in e.g. batteries (<a href=\"https://gist.github.com/Rob23oba/1cf9110aea1187650b548b747dca1aa3\">code</a>). The command is in principle similar to <code>run_cmd</code> except for one important difference: Variables from previous <code>#do</code> invocations are available in later invocations. So if there's some expensive computation you want to do once and then run stuff on, you can use <code>#do</code>, e.g.:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Command</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getPredicates</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MetaM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Array</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Name</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mut</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">names</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">nm</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">info</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getEnv</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">constants</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">isPrivateName</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">continue</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">isPropFormerType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">info</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">names</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">names</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">push</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nm</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">names</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">names</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">liftTermElabM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getPredicates</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">names</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">names</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">qsort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toString</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toString</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">logInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m!</span><span class=\"s2\">\"{names}\"</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">logInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m!</span><span class=\"s2\">\"{names.size}\"</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">unary</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">liftTermElabM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">names</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">filterM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">forallTelescopeReducing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getConstVal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nm</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">vars</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">vars</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">size</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">binary</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">liftTermElabM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">names</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">filterM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">forallTelescopeReducing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getConstVal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nm</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">vars</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">vars</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">size</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">logInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m!</span><span class=\"s2\">\"{unary}\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">logInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m!</span><span class=\"s2\">\"{binary}\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">logInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m!</span><span class=\"s2\">\"{unary.size}, {binary.size}\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>In this case, the <code>getPredicates</code> computation takes a while to complete and I want to analyze the result in several ways without having to rerun it again, e.g. sorting the list, filtering for unary or binary predicates, comparing the sizes, etc. If you just used <code>run_cmd</code>, then you'd have to either rerun the computation, know everything you want to do in advance, or store the result somewhere e.g. using copy-paste. But <code>#do</code> just allows you to easily use the old result. There's also <code>#do_meta</code> as an analogue for <code>run_meta</code> which I could've used here to avoid the <code>liftTermElabM</code>s.</p>",
        "id": 623893125,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1789321460
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I quite like the idea. I don't really have a use case for it at the moment but I would definitely show it to students next year. Let's turn Lean into a Jupyter notebook :-).<br>\nI wanted to ask: Is it possible to interleave function definitions &amp; <code>#do</code>? Something like</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">data</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getData</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">processData</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">data</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Data</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IO</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Processed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">processed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">processData</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">data</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 623894028,
        "sender_full_name": "Mirek Olšák",
        "timestamp": 1789322005
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Of course, <code>#do</code> is just a command like any other</p>",
        "id": 623894069,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1789322033
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Good. I was not sure if it couldn't be tricky to keep the variable context while updating the environment.</p>",
        "id": 623894181,
        "sender_full_name": "Mirek Olšák",
        "timestamp": 1789322098
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Well, the variable context is a part of the environment :-)</p>",
        "id": 623894221,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1789322116
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Does it mean that it lives across files? I am not sure if that should be expected.</p>",
        "id": 623894425,
        "sender_full_name": "Mirek Olšák",
        "timestamp": 1789322226
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>No it doesn't go that far</p>",
        "id": 623894454,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1789322242
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It's part of the environment but only the local environment; it isn't persisted into oleans</p>",
        "id": 623894488,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1789322259
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is this similar to your <code>#eval_set</code> you wrote here <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Persistent.20interactive.20data.3F/with/575353206\">https://leanprover.zulipchat.com/#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Persistent.20interactive.20data.3F/with/575353206</a> ?</p>",
        "id": 623901896,
        "sender_full_name": "Niels Voss",
        "timestamp": 1789326804
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"873547\">Robin Arnez</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/.60.23do.60.20command.20for.20reusing.20computations/near/623894221\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Well, the variable context is a part of the environment :-)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>How does this interact with linearity on the values that are being computed?</p>",
        "id": 623901981,
        "sender_full_name": "Henrik Böving",
        "timestamp": 1789326865
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"521331\">Niels Voss</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/.60.23do.60.20command.20for.20reusing.20computations/near/623901896\">schrieb</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Is this similar to your <code>#eval_set</code> you wrote here <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Persistent.20interactive.20data.3F/with/575353206\">https://leanprover.zulipchat.com/#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Persistent.20interactive.20data.3F/with/575353206</a> ?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Yes, indeed! It is essentially a generalization of <code>#eval_set</code> in that it lets you use arbitrary do elements instead just <code>let x &lt;- y</code> style assignment</p>",
        "id": 623902056,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1789326910
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"395550\">Henrik Böving</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/.60.23do.60.20command.20for.20reusing.20computations/near/623901981\">schrieb</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>How does this interact with linearity on the values that are being computed?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Well, linearity is not being preserved <em>at all</em> since all values are stored in the environment</p>",
        "id": 623902187,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1789326992
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>they probably also get marked multithreaded...</p>",
        "id": 623902223,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1789327006
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Exactly, that's what I was worried about</p>",
        "id": 623902247,
        "sender_full_name": "Henrik Böving",
        "timestamp": 1789327018
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah so you should probably avoid using non-persistent data structures in <code>#do</code>; but then again, these values are going to be copied at most once fully per <code>#do</code> so maybe we're still fine?</p>",
        "id": 623902484,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1789327129
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Anyways, persistent data structures are better for use in <code>#do</code>; or you know, just \"read-only\" variables</p>",
        "id": 623902572,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1789327166
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is the concern only that for Arrays, also their historical values are stored? (naturally, so Lean can replay them from any point in the file history) Or is there a deeper technical issue?</p>",
        "id": 623904397,
        "sender_full_name": "Mirek Olšák",
        "timestamp": 1789328307
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah I'm pretty sure that's the only concern</p>",
        "id": 623906838,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1789329876
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I would get use out of this!</p>",
        "id": 623908647,
        "sender_full_name": "Max Nowak 🐉",
        "timestamp": 1789330945
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I also want to highlight: Usually, commands get rerun even if only the trailing whitespace changes; this is not the case for <code>#do</code>! With <code>#do</code> I made sure that the vast majority of edits after the <code>#do</code> command won't cause it to re-elaborate. This is the first time I used incremental elaboration (the same thing that makes tactics not reelaborate), so I hope that I didn't introduce a subtle bug there... but at least it seems to work very well in testing</p>",
        "id": 623913738,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1789334455
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Alright, here we go: <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/pull/1962\">batteries#1962</a></p>",
        "id": 623925810,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1789343911
    }
]